From 57fbb232dc26dcfa2ba0a14522e19fa3f0f82065 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdoupe <1207041+rdoupe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:59:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Only expect a ConfigureNotify for
 _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS when the WM supports it.

Since "winex11: Serialize _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS changes by expecting
a ConfigureNotify.", moving a fullscreen window to another monitor sets
configure_serial and waits for the window manager to resize the window.
Window managers that don't list _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS in
_NET_SUPPORTED (Hyprland, sway and other wlroots XWayland WMs) ignore the
message and never send that ConfigureNotify. configure_serial then stays
set: the config request for the new rect is delayed forever, and
window_update_client_config() ignores every later ConfigureNotify, so the
Win32 window rect no longer follows the X11 window.

With emulated display modes this breaks input. A game that switches to
exclusive fullscreen on display 1 while the compositor keeps its window
on display 2 gets pointer positions mapped through display 1's scaling
(offset by the letterbox), and a ClipCursor() on its window rect pins the
pointer to the edge of display 1.

Only wait for the ConfigureNotify when the window manager supports
_NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS. Otherwise the config request goes out, the
window manager answers it with the rect it actually keeps, and the Win32
rect follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/window.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index cc3b6185..0f8af34b 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1403,7 +1403,10 @@ static void window_set_monitors( struct x11drv_win_data *data, const struct moni
         XSendEvent( data->display, DefaultRootWindow( data->display ), False,
                     SubstructureRedirectMask | SubstructureNotifyMask, &xev );
 
-        if (is_fullscreen)
+        /* a window manager that doesn't support _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS ignores the request and
+         * will never send the ConfigureNotify we would be waiting for, blocking any further config
+         * change. Let the config request go through instead, the window manager will answer it. */
+        if (is_fullscreen && is_net_supported( x11drv_atom(_NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS) ))
         {
             data->configure_serial = data->monitors_serial;
             data->pending_state.rect = data->rects.visible;
-- 
